 "Lateral rectus (abducens nerve) of one eye and medial rectus (oculomotor nerve) of the other.",
 [("Frontal eye field (destructive)", "Eyes deviate toward the lesion; cannot look voluntarily to the opposite side; vestibulo-ocular reflex intact; recovers in days", "contralateral"), ("Frontal eye field (irritative, seizure)", "Eyes and head turn away from the focus", "contralateral"), ("PPRF", "Loss of ipsilateral saccades; eyes deviate away from the lesion; oculocephalic reflex can still bring the eyes across", "ipsilateral"), ("Abducens nucleus", "Complete ipsilateral gaze palsy not overcome by the oculocephalic reflex, usually with an ipsilateral facial palsy", "ipsilateral"), ("MLF", "Internuclear ophthalmoplegia: the ipsilateral eye fails to adduct, the contralateral eye shows abducting nystagmus, convergence spared", "ipsilateral"), ("Abducens nucleus plus ipsilateral MLF", "One-and-a-half syndrome: only abduction of the contralateral eye survives", "ipsilateral")],
