 "Vertical extraocular muscles of both eyes through the oculomotor and trochlear nerves.",
 [("Posterior commissure / pretectum (pineal tumor, hydrocephalus, top of basilar)", "Up-gaze palsy with convergence-retraction nystagmus, lid retraction and light-near dissociation (Parinaud)", "bilateral"), ("riMLF (bilateral paramedian thalamomesencephalic infarct)", "Loss of down-gaze (and up-gaze) saccades with somnolence", "bilateral"), ("Progressive supranuclear palsy", "Slow then absent vertical saccades, down-gaze first, overcome by the oculocephalic reflex", "bilateral"), ("Oculomotor and trochlear nuclei or nerves", "Nuclear or infranuclear palsy: not overcome by head movement, with ptosis or diplopia", "n/a")],
 ["Up-gaze palsy: think dorsal midbrain compression. Down-gaze palsy: think riMLF or PSP", "A vertical gaze palsy overcome by the doll's-head maneuver is supranuclear", "Elderly patients often have limited up-gaze normally; down-gaze limitation is never normal"],
